A||N||7||Seanh||Would Anyone be interested in adding Perfomance sound without rewiring?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||10-01-2000||01:04 PM||||I have a question. I have done this somones car already, and I am in the process of doing it again. I am taking a factory amp, and since it is hard to get the plug that goes into the amp, cutting the plug out and making a new plug with three ends. One end will go to the amp, one to the radio, and one into the factory harness. That is how the factory Performance sound is hooked up, just further into the wiring then right behing the deck. It is a simple plug and play setup. Although it would be kind of pricy do to the fact that two adapters will have to be used. If I could get enough demand I would order bluk amounts of these harness' to cut the cost. I would have to sell them for $35.00 each, and it would require you sending me your amp. Or, I could get you an amp, but there about $80.00. You could look for an amp yourself, send it to me for the rewiring and adapter, and then I would send back to you for installation. You would need the Sub and subbox already. I cannot get these at all. Please let me know if you would be interested so I will know if I have enough demand to order them or not. It would not take me more then one day to rewire the amp and get it on its way back to you. This is a good chance for you if you want to add factory options or you have the system, but dont want to go to the trouble of rewiring the whole car.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
