Z||000003||286SE'S||10-02-2000||11:47 AM||||Amp plug hard to find? I see them all the time in junked TransAms with the Performance Sound option.  Should I be cutting them off and selling them on E-bay? <BR>Where are these amps and boxes and overhead control/light panel comming from that have no wiring? <BR>TransAms also use the same speakers but they all are suffering from cone rot too. Although I have the performance sound in both of my cars they are currently disconnected. Even after replacing the speakers they just honk and bloop with mucky distortion. <BR>My opinion on Performance sound is that is  just hype and not somthing you "just gotta have" to make your Fiero complete. I just started thinking that that big plastic box would be a great place to hide my car alarm electronics. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||10-02-2000||05:23 PM||||The amps I can get are brand new, they put out the same amount of power, same plugs, and same size, but all new. I live in a small town here and the junk yard here has not seen a Fiero for 4 years. I have never thought to look into the Firebirds. But if I recall correctly, they have 2 5 1/4" subs, right? The wiring should be pretty close, but there would be a small problem. I will have to look into it. Your performance sound, are you running an aftermarket headunit in your cars? It should sound pretty good, not as good as alot of aftermarket options for more money and a little trouble mounting them in the stock locations. <P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||10-03-2000||08:50 PM||||I notice that you have a plug going to the amp, one to the radio and one to the factory harness - didn't you forget about the overhead switch? The wiring runs from the overhead switch to a connector box under the top right side of the dash, then to the radio harness. The radio harness runs from the vehicle wiring harness to the radio and to the amp and then to the sub-woofer speaker. I have removed and installed quite a few of these now - it is fun to say the least, especially concerning the overhead switch wiring. I currently have an AM/FM'CD w/ equalizer from a '98 Grand Am in my two cars and am using the stock 15 watt amp with the stock 5 1/4" sub-woofer speaker and it puts out plenty of bass -- I rarely turn the slider switch aqll the way up.......<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                        <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||KRMFiero||10-04-2000||06:46 PM||||does anyone have any box plans/sizes for a Fiero... any Idead of where to put them?  thanx alot<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||10-04-2000||10:11 PM||||No, I didnt forget about the slider switch. I just forgot to mention it, I usally dont reccomend going to the trouble of putting it in the overhead lights unless you really want a factory look. I usally just put them beside the cigg. lighter, in front of the computer harness. I agree that little speaker is nothing compared to an after-market system, but for the money, it really adds alot to the stock setup. If Im not mistaken, that "box" under the dash, what is its point, I know the system is a variable 10K resister in series with a fixed 10K resistor, it that all the box is, the fixed res.? As far as box designes, there are alot of ways to go, depending on what and were you want it. You can put up to 2 10" upfront and port them into the car. 2 12's behind the seats. You could put an 8in under the dash in the stock location. Some people are putting 2 10's in a box in the rear window. I believe 80's Boy was going to try and do that. If you happen to read this, have you tried it yet? If you have, what did you find out, very good quality? You could also put a 10 in the passenger footwell, I am currently working on a design for that. I got the idea after seeing one in an Acura NSX at a sound competition. It only took 4"  away from the passenger foot well. I will let you guys know about how this works out. My car has the sub up front and ported into the car, so if it does work, Ill post the plans here and I will be selling them hopfully if anyone would be interested.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
